Abstract
The project aims to predict the academic performance of students using demographic, educational, and examination-related features. The workflow covers data preprocessing, exploratory data analysis, feature engineering, model development, model evaluation, and comparison.
Introduction
Educational institutions can use predictive analytics to identify students who may require academic support. This project demonstrates an end-to-end machine learning pipeline for predicting student performance.
Objectives
•	Analyze the dataset.
•	Clean and preprocess data.
•	Perform exploratory data analysis.
•	Feature Engineering and Selection
•	Build regression models.
•	Compare model performance.
•	Predict math student score.
Dataset Description
The dataset contains student demographic information, parental education, lunch type, test preparation status, and mathematics, reading, and writing scores. Math score, is used as the prediction target.
